  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAnother system is expected Sunday night into Monday. The system \nlooks to track just west or right over the area early Monday \nmorning, with a period of rain likely. Temperatures will be \nmild, so it is expected to be all rain Sunday night. Some cooler\nair will gradually filter into the area on Monday behind the \ncold front, so some of the lingering rain showers could perhaps \nmix with some wet snow flakes later Monday into Monday night \nbefore ending. Temperatures will still be mild in the mid-40s to\naround 50 on Monday though. It cools off into the upper 20s to \nlower 30s by Monday night.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure builds in from the west on Tuesday into Wednesday next \nweek, so other than some lingering lake effect rain and/or snow\nshowers on Tuesday, it should dry out under partly sunny skies \nwith seasonable temperatures.\n\nWe'll see a slight warming trend towards the end of the week as\nthe center high pressure propagates eastward, and southerly flow\nprovides the milder temperatures. Temperatures are currently\nforecasted to be in the low to mid 50s Thursday.",
